add(806,'unproved claim',[193],'104–125','X=∅ ⇔ r(X)=∅; X connexe ⇔ r(X) connexe','Under R1 and R2 the realization detects the initial object and connected objects.','Connected means noninitial with only trivial complementary decompositions.','agrees','This is a short proposition omitted from the Codex open-step list, captured from the full text.')
add(807,'self-flagged step',[193],'109–125','dégager en lemme de catégorie multigaloisienne','Define X subordinate to P when its pullback to P is constant on each rank stratum. The resulting full category is claimed stable under finite limits, finite colimits and summands; local subordination gives a substack.','The definition does not say P→1 is covering. The missing condition matters at217. For a Galois object, the usual covering/torsor convention supplies it.','agrees','The closure lemma is explicitly requested. We do not silently insert the covering hypothesis into the definition.')
