add(809,'self-flagged step',[193,195],'123–125;132–145','lemme à dégager; n’utilise pas l’hyp. galoisienne','The realization compares piecewise constant objects over P with piecewise constant schemes over r(P); for a G-Galois P this yields the equivariant classification, then an étale-local version.','Theorem1 includes local triviality after étale base change on S, and says this condition is automatic when r(P) is finite over S. The inserted finite in Proposition3 constrains the meaning of revêtements.','agrees','Neither arbitrary étale covers of unbounded fibres nor unrestricted left exactness of r is inferred.')
add(810,'unproved claim',[196],'146–161','R3 aussi. R4 aussi. O.K.','An admissible finite-group action on a scheme produces a ramification datum from equivariant covers that become piecewise constant locally on S, using quotient realization. With bounded ranks and S quasi-compact, global objects form a filtered union of Galois-generated subcategories.','A modern interpretation uses finite locally constant covers and quotient-stack descent. The source checks the axioms only in compressed sentences.','agrees','These are assertions said to work, not explicit questions, but belong in the claims map.')
