add(812,'unproved claim',[198],'174–200','φ est néc. pleinement fidèle','Morphisms of ramification data with fixed realizations are described by a Galois object and its equivariant realization; every such morphism is asserted fully faithful. Between quotient models, morphisms correspond to compatible torsors with quotient Z.','Full faithfulness concerns φ between ramification categories, not r into schemes. R2 and realization compatibility compare subobjects, giving the relevant exact-functor criterion.','agrees','This does not revive the cancelled194 faithfulness assertion about r.')
add(813,'unproved claim',[199,200],'201–228','on peut recoller; On vérifie que tt marche','Local models, equivalences on double overlaps, isomorphisms on triples and coherence on quadruples give gluing. A gerbe with a representation in schemes gives a ramification datum by equivariant finite covers and colimit realization.','The finite étale band and admissibility/existence of the represented quotients remain hypotheses. The modern quotient-stack reading is our interpretation.','agrees','The notes correctly distinguish “On vérifie” from “à vérifier”; this is an asserted construction, not an authorial doubt.')
add(814,'unproved claim',[200],'211–228','donnée de ramification kummérienne','Root equations t_i^{n_i}=a_i with n_i invertible define finite Kummer models with band product μ_{n_i}; varying the n_i is said to give a limiting datum.','Only finitely many n_i differ from1. A compatible category of finite covers/infinite root-stack interpretation is modern and requires a precisely chosen inverse/direct limit.','agrees','The displayed μ_n(S′)=∏μ_{n_i}(S) has a functoriality alarm; no ink correction is made.')
add(815,'self-flagged step',[201],'229–239','qui n’est autre, comme on devine, que la famille des classes','The gerbe of local divisor equations and their chosen n_i-th-root changes has band ∏μ_{n_i}; its neutrality obstruction is identified with the divisor classes in H².','Our Čech calculation identifies the gerbe with the root gerbe of O(D_i); the sign depends on the direction of comparison arrows. The root stack of a divisor with its section is a different stack.','agrees','The cohomology-class identification is guessed rather than proved on the page. It matches the101/103 extension/Chern programme at a precise intermediate object.')
add(816,'self-flagged step',[201],'240–244','on voudrait en fait que n_i soit premier aux car résiduelles de D_i seulement','The author wants invertibility only along D_i, rather than throughout S, and starts describing the equivariant-cover version.','For an effective Cartier divisor, the root stack of the pair is trivial off D_i and is Deligne–Mumford if n_i is invertible along D_i. The line-bundle root gerbe has stabilizer everywhere and requires fppf treatment when n_i is not globally invertible.','agrees','The example2 continuation is unfinished. The modern root-stack completion is labelled ours.')
